      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Religious conservative arguments often prioritize the absolute sanctity of human life, asserting that the deliberate ending of life is a direct violation of divine law, often rooted in the belief that life is a God-given trust to be protected unconditionally.\n\nIn contrast, religious liberal viewpoints often emphasize principles like compassionate love, the right to self-determination, and the inherent value of a good death for the individual.\n\nThese liberal arguments typically argue that in extreme, unbearable suffering, supporting the right to choose a peaceful end can align more strongly with the ultimate divine love for the individual in their full context of need and autonomy",
